    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners in Utah can finance a roof replacement through contractor-partnered lenders, home equity loans, personal loans, or government assistance programs.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "contractor-partnered lenders, home equity loans, personal loans, or government assistance programs"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Financing Options"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contractor Financing: Many local Utah roofers partner with lenders to offer monthly payment plans directly from their offices or via quick online applications. Programs often feature soft credit checks for pre-qualification, promotional 0% \"Same-As-Cash\" periods (6 to 12 months), or extended terms ranging from 12 to 180 months . Companies like Legacy Roofing provide instant pre-qualification tools, while others like Whitaker Roofing offer fixed-rate term choices.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Legacy Roofing",
                "link": "https://www.legacyroofingutah.com/financing"
              },
              {
                "text": "Whitaker Roofing",
                "link": "https://whitakerroofing.com/financing"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Home Equity Loans or HELOCs: Borrowing against your home's equity typically secures lower interest rates than unsecured personal loans because your property acts as collateral."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Unsecured Personal Loans: Home improvement loans through banks, credit unions, or online platforms provide a lump sum without requiring home equity, though rates depend on your credit profile."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Government Assistance: Low-income or elderly rural homeowners in Utah may qualify for repair loans or grants through the USDA Rural Development Section 504 Program to remove safety hazards.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "USDA Rural Development Section 504 Program",
                "link": "https://www.rd.usda.gov/programs-services/single-family-housing-programs/single-family-housing-repair-loans-grants/ut"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Homeowner's Insurance: If a storm or severe weather damaged your roof, file an insurance claim to cover replacement costs minus your deductible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down the best financing path, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Is this an insurance claim (storm/hail damage) or an out-of-pocket replacement?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What is your estimated project budget or square footage?"
          }
        ]
      },
